.TH smi-pki-sign-csr "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI PKI Command"
.SH NAME
smi-pki-sign-csr \- Sign a CSR with a CA certificate and key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-pki-sign-csr
.I CSR_FILE CA_CERT_FILE CA_KEY_FILE CERT_FILE DAYS EXT_FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Signs \fICSR_FILE\fR with the CA \fICA_CERT_FILE\fR and \fICA_KEY_FILE\fR into \fICERT_FILE\fR, valid \fIDAYS\fR days, applying \fIEXT_FILE\fR. The CA private key is only read, never created here.
It is a thin command line wrapper over the matching function in the file based PKI library
\fBpki.sh\fR, so each step of building a CA and signing certificates can be run and inspected
on its own. All material is passed as file names; the command fails if the underlying OpenSSL
operation fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-pki-ca-create (1),
.BR smi-pki-create-domain-cert (1),
.BR openssl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Imre Tabur <imre.tabur@mail.ee>
